Event Planning Platform
A platform where users can create, manage, and discover events in their local area.

Resources: Events, Venues, Attendees
Registered users can RSVP, view upcoming events, and create their own.
Admin users can manage event categories and moderate submissions.

Backend: Web API
Must be built using either .NET
Must be RESTful and database-driven, with a custom-designed schema.
Must implement token-based authentication (e.g., JWT).
Must include user registration, login, and logout.
The API must expose full CRUD endpoints for at least three separate resources (excluding user and authentication endpoints).
Certain endpoints must be protected, accessible only to authenticated users.
All data must be persisted using a relational database of your choice (e.g., SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc.).
All data received from the user must be validated on the backend, and adequate error messaging must be provided when invalid data is submitted

Frontend: React
Must be built using React.
Must be a fully responsive web application that:
Allows user to register, log in, and log out.
Interacts with all available API endpoints.
Handles errors gracefully (e.g., form validation, invalid request).
Must be branded with a custom name, logo, and use a clean, professional UI.
Must use CSS frameworks/libraries or custom styling